title: Payers › Workflow Builder › Published workflows and conflicts
route: /payers/summit?tab=builder
intro: Several workflows can be published for one payer, each for a service, request type, state, plan and dates. New Case picks the most specific one. When two are equally specific, neither is chosen: the builder names both and New Case flags it. A workflow for 'Any request type' is the payer's default and gives way to a specific one.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Publish or edit a workflow\nor change its Details"
process p1 "Each time the builder checks, it asks the same matching New Case uses:\nfor each service and request type the workflow covers, which published workflows fit?"
decision d1 "Does exactly one workflow win for every case it covers?"
process p2 "Nothing to say"
decision d2 "Do two or more fit equally well?"
toast t1 "Notice in the bar, in ochre:\n'Two published workflows are equally specific'\n'A and B both match Residential 3.5, initial authorization.\nNew case flags it and picks neither until one is changed.'"
process p3 "Neither workflow is chosen for those cases\nThe checks list the same on the workflow being published"
click c1 "Open 'Details' and narrow one of them\nServices, request type, state, plan, provider type or dates"
click c2 "Or archive one"
process p4 "The more specific workflow wins: one service beats every service,\none request type beats 'Any request type', a plan or state beats none"
decision d3 "Is the open workflow published?"
screen n1 "Notice 'Published version N is in force. Your changes are saved as a draft of version N+1,\nand publishing it replaces version N.'"
store st1 "First save makes a draft of the next version beside the published one\nThe published one keeps serving new cases until the draft is published"
screen n2 "Notice 'Published version N is still in force. This draft is version M and replaces it when published.'"
process p5 "In-progress cases keep the version they started with\nNew case says 'A newer version exists' and offers 'Review newer version', never switching it silently"
end e1 "The right workflow is in force for each kind of case"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Workflow › Default process and equal matches"

s1 --> p1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| p2 --> d3
d1 -->|No| d2
d2 -->|Yes| t1 --> p3 --> c1 --> p4
p3 --> c2 --> p4
d2 -->|No| p4
p4 --> d3
d3 -->|Yes| n1 --> st1 --> n2 --> p5 --> e1
d3 -->|No| p5
p3 --> g1
